course: dictionary
lesson: 15988
title: Utilisation: the formal word for use
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Utilisation is a formal word meaning the act of using something, especially in a practical or useful way. «The utilisation of rainwater kept the school garden green all summer.» The clue is the garden staying green: the rainwater was used well, for a useful purpose.
explain: You will meet utilisation in reports, science books and exam papers. «Energy utilisation at the school went down after the new lights were fitted.» Here it means how much energy is used, and how well.
explain: In your own writing, the simpler word «use» is usually better. «We use rainwater for the garden» says the same thing as «We make utilisation of rainwater for the garden», but it is clearer and shorter.
fact: Utilisation means the act of using something, especially making practical or good use of it.
fact: Utilisation is a noun, and it is uncountable, so you say «the utilisation of», not «utilisations».
fact: The American spelling is utilization, with a z.
fact: The verb to use in this formal way is utilise (US: utilize), as in «We utilise the sunshine to dry the washing.»
fact: In everyday talk, people say «use», which is easier to read and write.
exercise: «The factory improved its utilisation of heat, so less energy was wasted.» What does utilisation mean here? | *Using heat in a practical, useful way | Turning the heat up as high as it will go | Ignoring the heat completely | Measuring how hot the room is
exercise: «The class talked about the utilisation of old bottles to make plant pots.» What is another word for utilisation in this sentence? | breaking | hiding | *use | wasting
exercise: Why might a writer choose the word utilisation instead of use? | It only means playing games | *It sounds formal, as in a report or a science text | It means the opposite of use | It is a shorter, more casual word
test: «Energy utilisation at the school went down after the lights were fixed.» What does utilisation mean here? | *The amount and way energy is used | A new lamp that never breaks | Lights that are too bright to look at | A school trip to the power station
test: The American spelling of utilisation is... | utilisasion | *utilization | utilate | utility
exam: «The utilisation of the old warehouse as a sports hall saved the town money.» Which meaning fits best? | Knocking the building down for scrap | Leaving the building empty forever | Painting the building bright colours | *Using the building in a practical, useful way
